{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794735262,"nonce":"KLoPPoiH/T3Cqv7aCMjBJLMHvVA=","title":"hxn-gpu-gles: an OpenGL ES 3 driver for Android and other devices without Vulkan","message":"A driver library over EGL and OpenGL ES 3.0, for Android devices without Vulkan and for embedded Linux. Shaders are hxnsl's `GLSL_VERTEX` and `GLSL_FRAGMENT`, which are GLSL ES 3.00, and `GLSL_BINDINGS` names the uniform blocks and combined samplers each stage binds, so the driver binds by name to the units it assigns. No compute: hxnsl gives a compute shader `GLSL_MISSING`.\n\nShares its shader path with WebGL2, which runs the same GLSL ES 3.00.","files":null}]}